 {"id": "BT-83", "title": "gitleaks sk-api-key rule matches mid-word prose (word 'task-...' contains 'sk-'): tier1 secrets FAIL is a false positive, and the judge misattributes it to harness state", "status": "complete", "priority": "P2", "source": null, "created_by": "pm:boardctl", "created_at": "2026-10-30T22:34:58Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-31T04:31:22Z", "ts": null, "complexity": 2, "detail": {"fingerprint": "d1be17aef2b01b21fb942341067e6e4f956c7932ab27a4879fb04480d34a45ac", "evidence": [{"run_id": "boardctl-pm-2026-10-30-17-26-12", "ts": "2026-10-30T22:34:58Z"}, {"run_id": "boardctl-pm-2026-10-30-17-26-12", "ts": "2026-10-31T00:30:00Z", "note": "EVIDENCE REFRESH (same sk-api-key class, count drift 1 -> 5): `gitleaks detect --source . --no-git --config .gitleaks.toml --report-format json` now exits 1 with 5 findings, all rule sk-api-key: events.jsonl:584 (BT-81 closeout ch:trace prose tail), tasks.jsonl:198 (original repro line), tasks.jsonl:215 x3 (this row's own repro prose self-triggers). Filing-time count of exactly 1 is stale; the boundary fix must exit 0 on all 5. Verified by PM pre-add gate pass 2026-10-31."}]}, "reasoning": "The custom rule sk-api-key in .gitleaks.toml (regex (?i)sk-[a-zA-Z0-9_-]{20,}) has no word-boundary anchor, so it matches the sk- substring mid-word. Reproduced 2026-10-30: `gitleaks detect --source . --no-git --config .gitleaks.toml` reports exactly 1 finding = rule sk-api-key at .coding-hermes/board/tasks.jsonl line 198, matching the tail of the word task- in the closeout prose `verdict=none:task-complete-unavailable` (token length 23, sha256 b532af469103906e538de7e02b190c08ffafaa223102718632293f2929dfbf1d). This false positive FAILs the gitreins tier1 secrets step and flips overall judge verdicts to false on otherwise-green work: measured on RELEASE-2026-10-29-01 (.gitreins/history/2026-10-30/b4ae2b55/verdict.json: tier2 PASS/COMPLETE, tier1 secrets exit 1), and the BT-81 and QA-BOARDCTL-RELENG-2 closeout notes cite the same class. The verdict narrative 'harness state excluded from gitleaks scope (.gitreins/**)' is a misattribution: the finding is board prose in tasks.jsonl (allowlisted paths cover .gitreins/ already), and the guard log the verdict cites (.gitreins/logs/guard-20261030T205139.648389Z.log) is green ([PASS] secrets, 'gitleaks: clean'); the FAIL comes from the judge's own tree scan. BT-018 (complete) narrowed the allowlist but never anchored this rule; same mid-word FP class as the historical disk-emergency/sk-eme case. No open row owns this fix.", "review_notes": null, "acceptance_criteria": "1) The sk-api-key rule in .gitleaks.toml requires a non-alphanumeric boundary before sk- (RE2-safe prefix, e.g. (?:^|[^a-zA-Z0-9])sk-[a-zA-Z0-9_-]{20,} \u2014 no lookbehind), and `gitleaks detect --source . --no-git --config .gitleaks.toml` exits 0 with zero findings on the tree that contains the tasks.jsonl line-198 prose `verdict=none:task-complete-unavailable` (quote the exit code and the absence of a 'leaks found' line). 2) A regression test pins both sides: the pre-fix regex matches task-complete-unavailable while the fixed regex does not, and a boundary-delimited sk- token of 20+ chars is still caught; the test fails if the boundary fix is reverted, and `go test ./...` exits 0 with it in place. BT-018 doctrine holds: no new blanket path exclusion \u2014 docs/specs/Markdown stay scanned. 3) `gitreins guard` on the fixed tree prints [PASS] secrets, and the next `gitreins task complete` records tier1 secrets passed=true (`jq '.stages.tier1.passed' .gitreins/history/<date>/<run>/verdict.json` prints true) with the overall verdict no longer false on the secrets step; the closeout note records the corrected attribution (finding was mid-word board prose at tasks.jsonl:198, not .gitreins/** harness state)."}
 {"id": "BT-84", "title": "Repo hygiene: tracked generated artifacts churn the working tree (board-report.html rendered_at nondeterminism + .gitreins/logs runtime logs) \u2014 sweep commits recur (3f3dd16, 95dae4c)", "status": "complete", "priority": "P3", "source": null, "created_by": "pm:boardctl", "created_at": "2026-10-31T00:45:51Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-31T12:47:51Z", "ts": null, "complexity": 2, "detail": {"fingerprint": "75810e9592d8277eb19371c814897f368f1be454642c14dcbfa73734582d3be2", "evidence": [{"run_id":"boardctl-pm-2026-10-30-17-26-12","ts":"2026-10-31T00:45:51Z","tree_fp":"a4399ce760158e2e3ea6da687d0498aee7f7ecb4a4f65ce4d571d977a4f6f55a"},{"run_id":"ephemeral:bt-84-final-post-fix-acceptance","ts":"2026-10-31T12:44:34Z"}]}, "reasoning": "Measured 2026-10-31 by PM tick boardctl-pm-2026-10-30-17-26-12: git diff of cmd/boardctl/board-report.html is exactly one rendered_at timestamp change (2026-10-30T15:59:26-05:00 -> 17:03:06-05:00) on the fixture/demo board payload, so every render dirties a tracked file; 20 guard-run logs are tracked under .gitreins/logs/ and churn by addition/deletion (tracked deletion of guard-20261017T224112.241967Z.log still uncommitted; untracked guard-20261030T210710.998681Z.log arrived with tick 168). Sweep commits 3f3dd16 and 95dae4c already cleaned the same class and it recurred the same day. Harm: the shared product checkout is permanently dirty, which blocks clean-tree product-gate collection (PM verification rules: never report a product gate from a dirty shared checkout), and each sweep is pure toil. G7 dedup: no prior row owns this class \u2014 board-report mentions live in BT-020/BT-021/BT-022/BT-027/DOC-17/BT-81/RELEASE-2026-10-29-01 rows, all feature work; CLN-1 is a completed folder-structure cleanup.", "review_notes": null, "acceptance_criteria": "1) Artifact disposition decided per class and the tree proven stable: after `boardctl render -o cmd/boardctl/board-report.html` run twice back-to-back and one `gitreins guard` run, `git status --porcelain` reports zero modified/added/deleted lines for cmd/boardctl/board-report.html and .gitreins/logs/ (quote the command and its empty output). Each artifact class is either untracked+gitignored or byte-deterministic on regeneration; the disposition is recorded in the closeout note.\n2) Determinism pinned with hashes: if board-report.html stays tracked, two consecutive renders must produce identical sha256 (quote both hashes) e.g. rendered_at pinned/omitted via flag or excluded from the artifact; the 20 tracked .gitreins/logs/*.log entries are dispositioned in the same change (removed from the index with an ignore rule, or no longer emitted), and the live residue is gone at the end of the change: tracked deletion of .gitreins/logs/guard-20261017T224112.241967Z.log resolved and cmd/boardctl/board-report.html back to clean.\n3) No behavior regression and no toil left: `go build ./... && go vet ./... && go test ./...` exits 0 (quote exit codes), and no sweep-chore commit is required afterward \u2014 a fresh render + guard cycle leaves `git status --porcelain` empty so the recurring sweep class (3f3dd16, 95dae4c) cannot recur.", "worker_status": "complete", "foreman_note": "Foreman tick boardctl-foreman-2026-10-31-10-53-22: serial dispatch; premise verified live; worker glm-5.3-flash @ zai-glm.\n\nch:trace row=BT-84 spec=none:repo-hygiene wave=none:serial test=cmd/boardctl/render_test.go::TestCmdRenderDemoFixtureIsByteDeterministic,cmd/boardctl/bt077_render_roundtrip_test.go::TestExportImportRoundTripsAssociations doc=README.md prompt=/home/kara/.hermes/cache/scratch/boardctl-BT-84-retry-20261031.txt evidence=.gitreins/history/2026-10-31/cbb8272d/verdict.json witness=run:github-actions-exact-head-26afe69 verdict=ephemeral:bt-84-final-post-fix-acceptance commit=26afe6913fd7554393936adf46dd988eb49476ad memory=none:tick-local\n\nCloseout event 585 and header ticks_total 169 validated; legacy board warnings remain, no new BT-84 errors.", "worktree": "/home/kara/worktrees/boardctl-BT-84", "branch": "wt/BT-84", "commit_hash": "2a7ef7fd6f63d81eb7824f3fd79ea5ff19df8c6d", "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": "GREEN", "worker_summary": "Worker 2a7ef7f + merged 628d54f + post-fix d7ea140: .gitreins/logs ignored and 20 tracked runtime logs removed; tracked demo report deterministic; BT-077 render round-trip test now writes HTML to a temp path. Build/vet/full test and exact render+guard probes pass. Initial GitReins cap verdicts are preserved at .gitreins/history/2026-10-31/f6a1cd76, 032eee61, cbb8272d; final ephemeral post-fix acceptance PASS.", "completed_at": "2026-10-31 12:37:17"}
+{"id": "BT-85", "title": "Coverage floor gate: no Makefile target or CI step enforces test coverage (measured 82.9% total, 66.5-90.9% per package) \u2014 nothing stops silent coverage rot", "status": "pending", "priority": "P3", "source": null, "created_by": null, "created_at": "2026-11-03T18:50:09Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-03T18:50:09Z", "ts": null, "complexity": 3, "detail": {"fingerprint": "28900fe71396ec2acc45b29dea7c527856471e29aac13a08cd53d1d1c83b0fda"}, "reasoning": "Coverage floor gate: nothing enforces test coverage \u2014 measured 82.9% total / 66.5-90.9% per package today, and a package can drift to 0% with every gate green.\n\nMeasured 2026-11-03 (foreman discovery sweep, boardctl tick nudge2):\n  go test ./... -count=1 -short -cover  -> all packages ok\n  per package: cmd/boardctl 83.4, cmd/dedupe-board 76.0, cmd/gendocs 68.8, internal/board 83.5,\n               internal/describe 66.5, internal/fmtcheck 69.0, internal/freshness 84.8,\n               internal/render 90.9, internal/seccheck [no statements], internal/speccheck 88.0,\n               internal/versioncheck 83.6, internal/vulncheck 86.2, internal/workflowcheck 83.7\n  go tool cover -func coverage.out -> total 82.9% of statements\n  grep -c -i coverage README.md docs/**/*.md -> 0 (no documented coverage policy at all)\n  Makefile has fmt-check, version-check, spec-check, vuln-check, install-check \u2014 no cover target\n  .github/workflows/ci.yml runs build, vet, TestGofmt, TestVersioncheck, speccheck, govulncheck, go test -short \u2014 no coverage step\n\nHarm: the repo's quality stack gates formatting, release pins, spec parity and vulnerabilities, but NOT test\ncoverage. Any package (or every package) can lose coverage silently while build/vet/test/gofmt stay green; there is\nno documented floor, so a worker has no target to defend and a reviewer has nothing to compare against.\n\nG7 dedup: no prior row owns this class. BT-028 (gofmt), BT-030/BT-062 (version + spec parity), BT-033 (vuln) are the\nsibling gates \u2014 each one a checker package plus a Makefile target and CI step; none of them measures coverage.", "review_notes": null, "acceptance_criteria": "1) `make cover-check` EXISTS and passes at HEAD: it takes a real `-coverprofile` (go test ./... -count=1 -short -coverprofile=<tmp>) and enforces BOTH floors \u2014 total >= 80% and per-package >= 60% \u2014 with a named exempt list for statement-less packages (internal/secretscheck). Quote the command, its stdout summary (total + the lowest package) and exit 0.\n2) The gate is provably LOAD-BEARING, not decorative: forcing a floor above current coverage makes it exit non-zero and NAME the offending package with its percentage (e.g. `--min-package 95` -> exit 1 naming internal/describe 66.5%). Quote both the pass (exit 0) and the forced fail (exit 1 + the named package). A gate that cannot be shown failing is a FAIL.\n3) Unit tests cover the checker's own logic hermetically (synthetic coverage profiles in t.TempDir(), NO nested suite run): total below floor, one package below floor, exempt package ignored, empty/malformed profile -> error, and the exact-boundary case (a package at exactly the floor passes). `go test ./... -count=1` for the package green.\n4) CI carries the gate: a step in .github/workflows/ci.yml runs the SAME command as `make cover-check` (byte-identical flags), and the pushed run is completed/success with that step visible in `gh run view <id> --json jobs --jq '.jobs[].steps[]'`.\n5) No regression anywhere else: `go build ./... && go vet ./...`, `go test ./... -count=1` (full, not -short), `make fmt-check`, `make version-check`, `make spec-check`, `make vuln-check` all pass; `git status --porcelain` shows only intended files (no stray binary; cmd coverage binary must not be committed).\n6) The gate is DOCUMENTED and the documented command works: README (Development/gates section) names the target, both floors, and how to exempt a package (with a reason required), and the documented invocation was actually run and quoted. `make cover-check` must be listed alongside the existing fmt-check/version-check/spec-check/vuln-check.", "worker_status": "pending", "foreman_note": null, "worktree": null, "branch": null, "commit_hash": null, "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "worker_summary": null, "completed_at": null}
